# a hidden subunit's constant that has no value is reported at its definition,
# as a file unit's is. The subunit materialises on demand, after this unit's
# constant walk, and its constants were never resolved: the use below read a
# value that typed to nothing, an "Unknown reference 'wide'" pointing at a name
# that plainly exists
main: function is {
    print "\{words.scaled x: 1}"
}
